[6] Proof readout
  1. On the targeted residue-collision/control surface, closed
     danger-arc H1 occurs only on the AP/Goddyn-Wong boundary rows.
  2. The residue-terminal boundary/open collisions are therefore not only
     beta-separated; they have an explicit GF(2) boundary representative.
  3. The lightweight full-bank status scan gives zero mixed boundary/open
     fibers for the coarse ET+unit gate.  HYP-3030's route-mixed open
     survivors should be scheduled only after this path-boundary topology
     removes equality atoms.
  4. Deleting any owner speed from the displayed AP/GW representative
     kills the closed H1 signal in this carrier.  This is the old
     deletion-persistence idea, but applied to danger arcs instead of
     runner tournaments.
